'''WEIGHTS AND MEASURES.''' This subject may be most conveniently considered under three aspects—I. Scientific; II. Historical; and III. Commercial.

{{c|I. {{sc|Scientific}}}}

1. ''Units.''—In the United Kingdom two systems of weights and measures are now recognized—the imperial and the metric. The fundamental units of these systems are—of length, the yard and metre; and of mass, the pound and kilogram.

